-- title:
--   The Weierstrass cubic in all contact ideals
-- statement:
--   Let G be the stable elliptic-extension geometry and let z be outside its period lattice. Write v for the chart-0 coordinates at z, and q=X₂²−4X₁³+g₂X₁+g₃ for the affine Weierstrass cubic. Then
--
--   v₂²=4v₁³−g₂v₁−g₃,
--
--   and the principal ideal generated by q is contained in the chart contact ideal at v of every natural order N. Thus every contact-jet quotient at such a point, and every intersection of these contact ideals, imposes the same Weierstrass cubic relation.
--
--   The proof includes N=0. The non-lattice condition ensures the chart coordinates coincide with wp and wp-prime. No nonvanishing of wp-prime is assumed.
-- source:
--   Derived Weierstrass cubic contact-ideal step for https://prove2.me/theorems/efeea58b-7cef-4067-a43e-66959f6b78fa. Mission context: Senthil Kumar K (2026), Algebraic independence of values of Weierstrass elliptic and zeta functions, Appendix A.2, Theorem A.3 and Proposition A.1; https://doi.org/10.1017/S001309152610145X. This is a derived algebraic tool, not a completion of the zero estimate. Primary Lean sources: Mathlib Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Elliptic/Weierstrass.lean (PeriodPair.derivWeierstrassP_sq), RingTheory/Derivation/Basic.lean and the ideal span API, revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474. The initial affine coordinates satisfy the fixed Weierstrass cubic; tangency and the contact-ideal characterization propagate this relation to every jet order. This supplies the cubic in the intersection contact ideal and fixes the scalar first integral to minus g3.

import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassEllipticZeta_InterfaceGeometry
import Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination

noncomputable section
open WeierstrassEllipticZeta
open scoped Classical

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.chart_cubic_in_all_contact_ideals
    (G : Frontier.Geometry) (z : ℂ) (hz : z ∉ G.L.lattice) :
    let v := extensionChartCoordinates G.S 0 z
    let q := extensionChartCubic G.L.g₂ G.L.g₃ 0
    (v 2) ^ 2 = 4 * (v 1) ^ 3 - G.L.g₂ * v 1 - G.L.g₃ ∧
    ∀ N : ℕ, Ideal.span ({q} : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin 4) ℂ)) ≤
      extensionChartContactIdeal G.L.g₂ G.L.g₃ 0 v N := by sorry
